  "text": "סרטןıyor\nLet's denote \\( z = x + yi \\), where \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) are real numbers. Then, \\( z^2 = (x + yi)^2 = x^2 - y^2 + 2xyi \\) and \\( z(z - 3i) = (x + yi)(x + (y-3)i) = x^2 + xyi - 3xi + y(y-3) = x^2 + y(y-3) + (xy - 3x)i \\). Therefore, the given equation \\( |z^2 - 9| = |z(z - 3i)| \\) becomes:\n\n\\[\n|x^2 - y^2 - 9 + 2xyi| = |x^2 + y(y-3) + (xy - 3x - 3y)i|\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the magnitudes:\n\n\\[\n|(x^2 - y^2 - 9) + 2xyi| = \\sqrt{(x^2 - y^2 - 9)^2 + (2xy)^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n|x^2 + y(y-3) + (xy - 3x - 3y)i| = \\sqrt{(x^2 + y(y-3))^2 + (xy - 3x - 3y)^2}\n\\]\n\nUsing the given condition, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(x^2 - y^2 - 9)^2 + (2xy)^2} = \\sqrt{(x^2 + y(y-3))^2 + (xy - 3x - 3y)^2}\n\\]\n\nBy squaring both sides, we get:\n\n\\[\n(x^2 - y^2 - 9)^2 + (2xy)^2 = (x^2 + y(y-3))^2 + (xy - 3x - 3y)^2\n\\]\n\nExpanding both sides, we get:\n\n\\[\n(x^2 - y^2 - 9)^2 + 4x^2y^2 = (x^2 + y(y-3))^2 + (xy - 3x - 3y)^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n(x^4 - 2x^2y^2 + y^4 + 18x^2 + 18y^2 + 81) + 4x^2y^2 = (x^2 + y^2 - 3y)^2 + (x^2y - 3x^2 - 3xy + 9x + 9y)^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx^4 + y^4 + 18x^2 + 18y^2 + 81 + 2x^2y^2 = x^4 + y^4 + 6x^2y + 825x - 6y^3 + 87x^2 + 9x^2y - 27x^2y + 81\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[\n18x^2 + 18y^2 + 81 + 2x^2y^2 = 825x - 6y^3 - 6xy^2 + 87x^2 + 9x^2y\n\\]\n\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n-64x^2 - 6y^3 + 81 - 6xy^2 - 2x^2y^2 - 810x + 87y^2 + 6xy^2 - 6y^3 = 0\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-64x^2 - 12y^3 + 81 - 810x + 87y^2 - 2x^2y^2 = 0\n\\]\n\nThis is a complicated equation. Let's try to find simple values for \\( x \\) and \\( y \\). Considering the equation \\( |z - 2i| = \\sqrt{x^2 + (y-2)^2} \\), we need to minimize this expression. Let's try \\( x = 0 \\). Then, the equation simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n|z^2 - 9| = |z(z - 3i)|\n\\]\n\n\\[\n|z + 3i|^2 = |z - 2i|^2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n|z^2 - 9|^2 = |(z - 2i)(z + 2i)|\n\\]\n\n\\[\n|z|^2 - 9^2 = |z|^2 - 4iz^2 - 2iz + 4iz + 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\n|z^2 - 81| = 4\n\\]\n\nThis implies:\n\n\\[\n|z|^2 - 81 = 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\n|z|^2 = 85\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( |z| = \\sqrt{85} \\). The smallest possible value of \\( |z - 2i| \\) is when \\( z \\) is on the circle with radius \\( \\sqrt{85} \\) centered at the origin, and \\( |z - 2i| \\) is minimized when \\( |z| = \\sqrt{85} \\) and \\( z \\) is on the line perpendicular to the line connecting the origin and \\( 2i \\). This occurs when \\( |z - 2i| = \\sqrt{85 - 4} = \\sqrt{81} = 9 \\).\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of \\( |z - 2i| \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
